# SSH allowed-signers file for verifying signed git tags in CI.
# Format: <email> <namespaces> <ssh-pubkey>
# See: https://git-scm.com/docs/git-config#Documentation/git-config.txt-gpgsshallowedSignersFile
#
# Maintainer setup (one-time):
#   1. Generate an SSH signing key if you don't have one:
#        ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "git-signing"
#   2. Append your public key here, e.g.:
#        guy.godfroy@ovhcloud.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...XYZ
#   3. Configure your local git:
#        git config --global gpg.format ssh
#        git config --global user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
#        git config --global tag.gpgsign true
#   4. Sign tags going forward:
#        git tag -s vX.Y.Z -m "release X.Y.Z"
#
# Until at least one signer is listed, the release-apk job will fail at the
# verify-tag step and no release artifact will be published. This is the
# intended gate.
